     "id": "1524a302-b346-4e58-9a78-5743064a43ab",
     "prompt": "For the cubic graph $y=x^3$, what is the value of $y$ when $x=-2$?",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "$8$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$-6$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$-8$",
       "correct": true
      },
      {
       "text": "$4$",
       "correct": false
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "Substitute $x=-2$: $y=(-2)^3=(-2)\\times(-2)\\times(-2)=-8$."
    },
    {
     "id": "1007b500-e278-4021-b592-0c65b560d67c",
     "prompt": "Which point lies on the reciprocal graph $y=\\frac{12}{x}$?",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "$(3,4)$",
       "correct": true
      },
      {
       "text": "$(4,2)$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$(6,3)$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$(12,12)$",
       "correct": false
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "For $y=\\frac{12}{x}$, the coordinates must satisfy $xy=12$. For $(3,4)$, $3\\times4=12$."
    },
    {
     "id": "c53e664a-d0f8-40a5-9306-61945a3800df",
     "prompt": "Which statement about the graph $y=\\frac{1}{x}$ is correct?",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "It crosses both coordinate axes.",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "It crosses the $x$-axis but not the $y$-axis.",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "It crosses the $y$-axis but not the $x$-axis.",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "It approaches both coordinate axes but never touches them.",
       "correct": true
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "The axes are asymptotes. The graph approaches $x=0$ and $y=0$, but $x$ cannot equal $0$ and $\\frac{1}{x}$ can never equal $0$."
    },
    {
     "id": "946f4e95-5102-48aa-a6b4-77572f6c430e",
     "prompt": "What is the $y$-coordinate of the point on $y=x^3-2$ when $x=2$?",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "$4$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$6$",
       "correct": true
      },
      {
       "text": "$8$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$10$",
       "correct": false
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "Substitute $x=2$: $y=2^3-2=8-2=6$."
    },
    {
     "id": "c326a1d1-c79e-4203-b11a-21206b2ee734",
     "prompt": "A point on the reciprocal graph $y=\\frac{6}{x}$ has $y$-coordinate $-3$. What is its $x$-coordinate?",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "$-18$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$-3$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$-2$",
       "correct": true
      },
      {
       "text": "$2$",
       "correct": false
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "Solve $-3=\\frac{6}{x}$. Multiplying by $x$ gives $-3x=6$, so $x=-2$."
